"question": "How has the visualization of traffic flow theory and highway capacity analysis evolved in civil engineering education, from time-space diagrams and manual traffic count sheets to microsimulation animations and real-time data dashboards? I'm interested in examining how textbooks, laboratory exercises, and student projects have represented congestion patterns, level of service concepts, and intersection operations through different visual media."
}
